tion is: for a given R and the constraint (1+t)(1+x) = R^25,\nwhat is the maximum possible z?\n\nGiven (1+t)(1+x) = P (fixed), z = c^2*(1+t)^2/(1+x)^2 = c^2*(1+t)^2*((1+t)/P)^2\nWait: (1+x) = P/(1+t), so z = c^2*(1+t)^2 * (1+t)^2/P^2 = c^2*(1+t)^4/P^2\nz is unbounded as c -> inf or (1+t) -> inf (with (1+x) = P/(1+t) -> 0)\n\nBUT WAIT: x >= 0 means (1+x) >= 1, so (1+t) <= P.\nAlso c > 0 is unbounded (c can be anything).\nSo z = c^2*(1+t)^2/(1+x)^2 is UNBOUNDED due to c being free.\n\nTHIS MEANS: for R > 50.517, there exist c large enough to make L2 < 0!\n\nNumerical verification: does L2 actually go negative?\n\nAt t=2.44e+42, x=1.0, c=1.0: L2 = -5.03470704212271e-06\n  NEGATIVE! c=2.0, P=10^50, R=100.00, L2=-1.5043e-101\n  NEGATIVE! c=2.0, P=10^60, R=251.19, L2=-1.0803e-120\n  NEGATIVE! c=5.0, P=10^50, R=100.00, L2=-7.1951e-100\n  NEGATIVE! c=5.0, P=10^60, R=251.19, L2=-4.6350e-119\n  NEGATIVE! c=10.0, P=10^50, R=100.00, L2=-1.1558e-98\n  NEGATIVE! c=10.0, P=10^60, R=251.19, L2=-7.4295e-118\n\nTesting with asymmetric t,x (large t, small x) and large c:\n  c=1.0, t=10^10, x=0, R=2.5119, z=1.00e+20, L2=1.7773e-03\n  c=1.0, t=10^20, x=0, R=6.3096, z=1.00e+40, L2=2.5940e-03\n  c=1.0, t=10^30, x=0, R=15.8489, z=1.00e+60, L2=3.2241e-03\n  c=1.0, t=10^40, x=0, R=39.8107, z=1.00e+80, L2=1.5780e-03\n  c=1.0, t=10^50, x=0, R=100.0000, z=1.00e+100, L2=-1.1559e-02\n  c=10.0, t=10^10, x=0, R=2.5119, z=1.00e+22, L2=1.7773e+01\n  c=10.0, t=10^20, x=0, R=6.3096, z=1.00e+42, L2=2.5940e+01\n  c=10.0, t=10^30, x=0, R=15.8489, z=1.00e+62, L2=3.2241e+01\n  c=10.0, t=10^40, x=0, R=39.8107, z=1.00e+82, L2=1.5780e+01\n  c=10.0, t=10^50, x=0, R=100.0000, z=1.00e+102, L2=-1.1559e+02\n  c=100.0, t=10^10, x=0, R=2.5119, z=1.00e+24, L2=1.7773e+05\n  c=100.0, t=10^20, x=0, R=6.3096, z=1.00e+44, L2=2.5940e+05\n  c=100.0, t=10^30, x=0, R=15.8489, z=1.00e+64, L2=3.2241e+05\n  c=100.0, t=10^40, x=0, R=39.8107, z=1.00e+84, L2=1.5780e+05\n  c=100.0, t=10^50, x=0, R=100.0000, z=1.00e+104, L2=-1.1559e+0