{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_bdrk_01WSaWH8E9CYD68fZMb9HjYM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ty5zf2bpPiJaVWVrPf9h5n","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"source ~/anaconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh 2>/dev/null || source ~/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh 2>/dev/null || source /opt/conda/etc/profile.d/conda.sh 2>/dev/null; conda activate wave && python3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport sympy as sp\n\nprint(\"=== SUFFICIENT CONDITION: Rigorous verification ===\")\nprint()\n\n# We showed: L1^2 - L^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 = (phi^2/2500^2) * Q(u,v)\n# where Q(u,v) = 2400*u^2 + 4803*u*v + 2400*v^2\n# with u = 1/(1+t)^2 > 0, v = c^2/(1+x)^2 > 0\n\n# The discriminant of the quadratic form is:\n# For Q(u,v) = A*u^2 + B*u*v + C*v^2 to be positive definite,\n# we need A > 0, C > 0, and B^2 - 4AC < 0\n# (This is the standard criterion for a 2-variable quadratic form)\n\nA = 2400\nB = 4803\nC = 2400\n\ndisc = B**2 - 4*A*C\nprint(f\"A = {A}, B = {B}, C = {C}\")\nprint(f\"B^2 = {B**2}\")\nprint(f\"4AC = {4*A*C}\")\nprint(f\"disc = B^2 - 4AC = {disc}\")\nprint()\n\nif disc > 0:\n    print(f\"WARNING: Discriminant = {disc} > 0, so the form is NOT positive definite!\")\n    print()\n    \n    # But we need to check: for u, v > 0, is Q(u,v) > 0?\n    # Q(u,v) = 2400u^2 + 4803uv + 2400v^2\n    # Since u, v > 0, all three terms are positive!\n    # 2400u^2 > 0, 4803uv > 0, 2400v^2 > 0\n    # So Q(u,v) > 0 for all u, v > 0.\n    print(\"However, since u > 0 and v > 0 (strictly):\")\n    print(\"  2400*u^2 > 0  (always)\")\n    print(\"  4803*u*v > 0  (since u > 0 and v > 0)\")\n    print(\"  2400*v^2 > 0  (always)\")\n    print()\n    print(\"ALL THREE TERMS ARE STRICTLY POSITIVE when u > 0 and v > 0!\")\n    print(\"Therefore Q(u,v) = 2400u^2 + 4803uv + 2400v^2 > 0 for all u,v > 0.\")\n    print()\n    print(\"Note: The positive-definiteness criterion (disc < 0) is for ALL real u,v.\")\n    print(\"But we only need positivity for u > 0, v > 0, which is trivially true\")\n    print(\"since all coefficients A, B, C are positive.\")\n    print()\n    print(\"=> L1^2 - L^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 > 0 for all x,t >= 0, c > 0  QED\")\n    print()\n    print(\"This proof is rigorous: no assumptions needed beyond u,v > 0.\")\n\nprint()\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\nprint(\"=== SUMMARY OF CONDITION STATUSES ===\")\nprint(\"=\" * 60)\nprint()\nprint(\"Condition 1a (L - L1 >= 0): TRUE\")\nprint(\"  Proof: L - L1 = (24c^2(1+t)^2 + 25(1+x)^2) / D, with D > 0\")\nprint(\"  Numerator is sum of positive terms.\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Condition 1b (-L1 - L >= 0): TRUE\")\nprint(\"  Proof: -L1 - L = (25c^2(1+t)^2 + 24(1+x)^2) / D, with D > 0\")\nprint(\"  Numerator is sum of positive terms.\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Condition 1: TRUE (both 1a and 1b hold)\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Condition 2 (lim lambda*psi = +inf): TRUE\")\nprint(\"  lambda*psi = (1/50)*log((1+t)(1+x)) -> +inf as x -> +inf\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Condition 3 (L2 >= 0): FALSE\")\nprint(\"  L2 becomes negative when R = ((1+t)(1+x))^(1/25) > 50.517\")\nprint(\"  This requires (1+t)(1+x) > 50.517^25 ≈ 3.86e42\")\nprint(\"  Concrete counterexample: t = 10^50, x = 0, c = 1 gives L2 < 0\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Sufficient condition: TRUE\")\nprint(\"  L1^2 - L^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 = (phi^2/2500^2) * (2400u^2 + 4803uv + 2400v^2)\")\nprint(\"  All coefficients positive, u > 0, v > 0 => strictly positive.\")\n\nPYEOF","description":"Final verification of sufficient condition and summary","timeout":120000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6803,"cache_read_input_tokens":118083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6803,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b069bf26-78c7-42ab-9d70-e5fa06956986","uuid":"f5c33b32-0157-42a4-a345-5cba12d101eb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ty5zf2bpPiJaVWVrPf9h5n","type":"tool_result","content":"=== SUFFICIENT CONDITION: Rigorous verification ===\n\nA = 2400, B = 4803, C = 2400\nB^2 = 23068809\n4AC = 23040000\ndisc = B^2 - 4AC = 28809\n\nWARNING: Discriminant = 28809 > 0, so the form is NOT positive definite!\n\nHowever, since u > 0 and v > 0 (strictly):\n  2400*u^2 > 0  (always)\n  4803*u*v > 0  (since u > 0 and v > 0)\n  2400*v^2 > 0  (always)\n\nALL THREE TERMS ARE STRICTLY POSITIVE when u > 0 and v > 0!\nTherefore Q(u,v) = 2400u^2 + 4803uv + 2400v^2 > 0 for all u,v > 0.\n\nNote: The positive-definiteness criterion (disc < 0) is for ALL real u,v.\nBut we only need positivity for u > 0, v > 0, which is trivially true\nsince all coefficients A, B, C are positive.\n\n=> L1^2 - L^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 > 0 for all x,t >= 0, c > 0  QED\n\nThis proof is rigorous: no assumptions needed beyond u,v > 0.\n\n============================================================\n=== SUMMARY OF CONDITION STATUSES ===\n============================================================\n\nCondition 1a (L - L1 >= 0): TRUE\n  Proof: L - L1 = (24c^2(1+t)^2 + 25(1+x)^2) / D, with D > 0\n  Numerator is sum of positive terms.\n\nCondition 1b (-L1 - L >= 0): TRUE\n  Proof: -L1 - L = (25c^2(1+t)^2 + 24(1+x)^2) / D, with D > 0\n  Numerator is sum of positive terms.\n\nCondition 1: TRUE (both 1a and 1b hold)\n\nCondition 2 (lim lambda*psi = +inf): TRUE\n  lambda*psi = (1/50)*log((1+t)(1+x)) -> +inf as x -> +inf\n\nCondition 3 (L2 >= 0): FALSE\n  L2 becomes negative when R = ((1+t)(1+x))^(1/25) > 50.517\n  This requires (1+t)(1+x) > 50.517^25 ≈ 3.86e42\n  Concrete counterexample: t = 10^50, x = 0, c = 1 gives L2 < 0\n\nSufficient condition: TRUE\n  L1^2 - L^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 = (phi^2/2500^2) * (2400u^2 + 4803uv + 2400v^2)\n  All coefficients positive, u > 0, v > 0 => strictly positive.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b069bf26-78c7-42ab-9d70-e5fa06956986","uuid":"f0fad755-17c4-4463-8e2b-bfde0b3dca22","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== SUFFICIENT CONDITION: Rigorous verification ===\n\nA = 2400, B = 4803, C = 2400\nB^2 = 23068809\n4AC = 23040000\ndisc = B^2 - 4AC = 28809\n\nWARNING: Discriminant = 28809 > 0, so the form is NOT positive definite!\n\nHowever, since u > 0 and v > 0 (strictly):\n  2400*u^2 > 0  (always)\n  4803*u*v > 0  (since u > 0 and v > 0)\n  2400*v^2 > 0  (always)\n\nALL THREE TERMS ARE STRICTLY POSITIVE when u > 0 and v > 0!\nTherefore Q(u,v) = 2400u^2 + 4803uv + 2400v^2 > 0 for all u,v > 0.\n\nNote: The positive-definiteness criterion (disc < 0) is for ALL real u,v.\nBut we only need positivity for u > 0, v > 0, which is trivially true\nsince all coefficients A, B, C are positive.\n\n=> L1^2 - L^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 > 0 for all x,t >= 0, c > 0  QED\n\nThis proof is rigorous: no assumptions needed beyond u,v > 0.\n\n============================================================\n=== SUMMARY OF CONDITION STATUSES ===\n============================================================\n\nCondition 1a (L - L1 >= 0): TRUE\n  Proof: L - L1 = (24c^2(1+t)^2 + 25(1+x)^2) / D, with D > 0\n  Numerator is sum of positive terms.\n\nCondition 1b (-L1 - L >= 0): TRUE\n  Proof: -L1 - L = (25c^2(1+t)^2 + 24(1+x)^2) / D, with D > 0\n  Numerator is sum of positive terms.\n\nCondition 1: TRUE (both 1a and 1b hold)\n\nCondition 2 (lim lambda*psi = +inf): TRUE\n  lambda*psi = (1/50)*log((1+t)(1+x)) -> +inf as x -> +inf\n\nCondition 3 (L2 >= 0): FALSE\n  L2 becomes negative when R = ((1+t)(1+x))^(1/25) > 50.517\n  This requires (1+t)(1+x) > 50.517^25 ≈ 3.86e42\n  Concrete counterexample: t = 10^50, x = 0, c = 1 gives L2 < 0\n\nSufficient condition: TRUE\n  L1^2 - L^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 = (phi^2/2500^2) * (2400u^2 + 4803uv + 2400v^2)\n  All coefficients positive, u > 0, v > 0 => strictly positive.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false}}
